findings_fixed.reasoning:
In lines 166-167:
```javascript
if (typeof series[serie] === "undefined") series[serie] = Object.create(null);
series[serie][xVal] = val;
```
If `serie` is `__proto__`, `series[serie]` accesses the prototype of the `series` object. While `series` is created with `Object.create(null)`, the assignment `series[serie][xVal] = val` still targets the prototype if `serie` is a built-in property name like `__proto__` or `constructor` that exists on the prototype chain of the target object. Although `Object.create(null)` mitigates the most common prototype pollution vectors by removing the prototype chain from the `series` object itself, the logic remains dangerous if the input `serie` is used to access or set properties on objects that are not strictly null-prototype objects.

